            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 90-year-old male patient, admitted on 11/10/2025 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, the patient presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed an acute exacerbation. Blood tests revealed mild inflammatory markers. During his short inpatient stay, the patient was treated with inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, resulting in satisfactory clinical improvement. Vital signs were closely monitored throughout. The patient was discharged in stable condition on 12/10/2025 with a prescription for oral steroids, bronchodilators, and instructions for follow-up. Please ensure continued COPD monitoring and medication review at your earliest convenience.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
